{title: Cinder Lane}
{artist: Mabel Orrin}
{key: G}
{capo: 2}

{comment: Tuning: Standard}

{comment: Strumming: D D U U D U}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Cinder lane is qui[C]et when the shutters close
[G]Lamplight on the co[D]bbles where the river goes
[G]Every window keeps [C]a story of its own
[Em]I keep mine fo[D]lded where t[G]he wind has blown
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Walk me down to [G]Cinder Lane
[D]Hold the lantern th[Em]rough the rain
[C]Walk me down to [G]Cinder Lane
[D]I will find my way aga[G]in
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Bakers at the corne[C]r and the milk cart bell
[G]Children trading mar[D]bles by the wishing well
[G]Every face is someo[C]ne that I used to know
[Em]Every step a pr[D]omise that I [G]made long ago
{end_of_verse}
